{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfXgeSF7RXgzdJcRtJsjj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The small-sample test is a tough regime for selection, but at production scale with 8000 validation rows, the simulation shows selection worked cleanly, picking 0.3 and landing close to the best-single result. I'm now weighing concerns like CPU time for the run.\n\nRunning the numbers, 4 candidates at ~74s plus overhead lands around 76s, giving ~37% headroom under a 120s ceiling, and the 100s budget guard would correctly bail out on later candidates if any single one runs long — I traced through scenarios at 30s and 50s per candidate to confirm the guard triggers appropriately either way. I'm also considering trimming to 3 candidates instead of 4, since the wd=3.0 candidate mainly matters at small sample sizes, and ordering candidates by prior likelihood could reduce wasted computation at larger scales.\n\nLooking at how optimal wd shifts with dataset size — roughly halving per doubling of n, dropping toward 0.1–0.2 by 80000 rows — the ordering [0.3, 0.1, 1.0, 3.0] seems reasonable to prioritize likely winners first. I'm also checking the ensemble gating thresholds and noise_rate sensitivity, comparing how different noise levels affect accuracy at both the small sample and the full 80k synthetic run.\n\nOther considerations: standardization correctly includes only appropriate columns, memory footprint at this scale is negligible, and rare classes that vanished under high wd should resurface with more data and lower regularization. I'll keep the learning rate fixed at 0.003 since I can't validate tuning it further at scale on real data.\n\nI want to run a couple more end-to-end sanity checks — one on synthetic data with a different seed, and one with a harder separation value to confirm the selection logic holds up. Then I'll finalize by copying the training script into place, updating the config and README, writing the report, and testing the exact production command with a sample test set to verify output shape and dtype.\n\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":118,"cache_read_input_tokens":84168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":118,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29d5ac31-0315-41dd-9b00-6d2c9a200a16","uuid":"9b1a125e-ab71-4d85-98d8-873668d0f63c","timestamp":"2026-09-29T11:53:34.367Z"}
